TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Failed checkpoint cp-weights because its fixed command mutates tracked receipts on every run, which no in-task retry can cure: the driver rejected the run with \"checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\" (exit 1), and the worktree diff shows only the `ts` fields of results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json (2026-08-29T12:47:30 -> 2026-08-30T07:25:28) and results/receipts/weights-worker.json (-> 2026-08-30T07:06:56) changing while shards=131 and bytes=185563854698 stayed identical on both nodes, confirming overseer steer #4's measured fact that the ~185.6 GB staging is already complete and was merely re-measured. Root cause is a defect in the checkpoint script pair, not in this task's execution. scripts/stage-weights.sh already carries the correct idempotence guard: it loads the receipt at the path it is handed and exits 0 without rewriting when status/shards/bytes match. But scripts/stage-weights-both.sh hands it a fresh mktemp path ($TMP/weights-coordinator.json, and the scp'd $TMP/weights-worker.json for the remote leg), so the guard's json.load always raises OSError on a nonexistent file, the fallthrough stamps time.strftime(\"%FT%T\"), and install_receipt then mv's that freshly stamped file over the committed tracked receipt. The guard is therefore dead code in the only path that reaches tracked files, and the same rewrite will recur on attempt 2 with a different timestamp. Fixing it requires editing scripts/stage-weights-both.sh (compare-then-install: skip the mv when the staged receipt's status/shards/bytes equal the committed receipt's, or seed the temp path from the committed receipt before invoking stage-weights.sh, and route the remote leg through the same comparison). cp-weights is kind=checkpoint with a worklist-fixed argv and a brief that forbids repository modification, so that source fix lies outside this task's authority and checkpoint tasks do not retry; this is blocked pending an amendment task that owns the script. Note also that the earlier checkpoint gate node for cp-weights recorded verdict=pass/exitCode=0 at witnessSeq 7885, so the underlying staging facts are sound and only the purity defect is outstanding.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","goal":"Make the both-nodes staging checkpoint a pure validator: re-running `bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh` against the already-correct prepared base (131 shards, 185563854698 bytes on coordinator and worker) must re-measure, compare against the committed receipts, leave results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json byte-identical (no fresh `ts` on an unchanged measurement), and exit 0. Repair scripts/stage-weights-both.sh so the idempotence guard already present in scripts/stage-weights.sh actually reaches the tracked receipts: today the wrapper stages each node's receipt into a fresh mktemp path, so the guard's json.load of that path always fails, a new time.strftime timestamp is always written, and install_receipt then mv's the restamped file over the committed receipt. Preferred shape: either seed the temp path with a copy of the committed receipt before invoking stage-weights.sh, or have install_receipt compare the staged receipt's status/shards/bytes to the committed one and skip the mv when they match. Apply the same treatment to the worker leg, whose receipt arrives via scp from /tmp/fn-weights-receipt.json. Preserve existing behavior on genuine drift (differing shards/bytes must still rewrite the receipt) and preserve the D12 fail-receipt quarantine under results/receipts/failed/. Do not re-copy the weights; the transfer is complete on both nodes. Land the change plus a short deterministic note as one non-empty commit inside the owned paths per the standing no-empty-squash note.","paths":["scripts/stage-weights-both.sh","scripts/stage-weights.sh","results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json","results/receipts/weights-worker.json"],"acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"rerun-leaves-tracked-receipts-clean","description":"Starting from a clean worktree, running the checkpoint command against the already-staged base leaves every tracked file byte-identical and exits 0.","argv":["bash","-c","git diff --quiet && bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh && git diff --exit-code -- results/receipts"]},{"id":"receipt-timestamps-unchanged","description":"The committed receipts still carry their original measurement timestamps after a re-run; no fresh stamp is applied to an unchanged measurement.","argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh >/dev/null && git diff --exit-code -- results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json results/receipts/weights-worker.json"]},{"id":"facts-still-match-staged-trees","description":"Both receipts report status pass with 131 shards and 185563854698 bytes, matching the staged trees on coordinator and worker.","argv":["python3","-c","import json;\nfor h in ('coordinator','worker'):\n r=json.load(open('results/receipts/weights-%s.json'%h));\n assert r['status']=='pass' and r['data']['shards']==131 and r['data']['bytes']==185563854698, (h, r)\nprint('receipts consistent')"]},{"id":"guard-reaches-tracked-receipts","description":"The wrapper no longer unconditionally moves a freshly stamped temp receipt over the committed one; the comparison or seeding step is present in scripts/stage-weights-both.sh.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -nE 'seed|already|unchanged|identical|cmp|compare' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"]},{"id":"drift-still-rewrites","description":"Genuine drift in shards or bytes still rewrites the receipt and surfaces as a tracked change rather than being silently suppressed.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -nE 'shards|bytes' scripts/stage-weights.sh scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"]},{"id":"fail-quarantine-preserved","description":"The D12 quarantine path for fail receipts under results/receipts/failed/ is still honored by install_receipt.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -n 'results/receipts' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh; grep -n 'failed' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"]}],"dependencies":[]}}
